The Anglican Way is a way of following Jesus that is rooted in Scripture, shaped by historic Christian worship, and lived out in everyday life. It brings together Word and Sacrament, reverence and joy, ancient faith and present hope. Through the prayers of the Church, the reading of Scripture, and gathering at the Lord’s Table, Anglicans are formed over time in the life of Christ. It is a steady, beautiful, and deeply biblical path that connects us to the historic Church while grounding us in grace today.
